Give refinements and commits their own pages, and fix three counts

Refinements and commits were two more cards inside the ledger page. Each now
has a page of its own:

- 改进记录: one row per refinement, newest first, with its scope, how many
  edits it made, and a chip per edit (create/update + memory/prompt/skill +
  title). Clicking a row opens the full record -- rationale, expected outcome
  and every edit's body -- fetched from `/api/refinement` on demand. The
  detail payload carries titles only: 28 records hold 117 KB of edit text and
  that would be paid on every session click.
- 提交: the `git_state` snapshots, deduplicated by commit, with branch, time,
  and the gap to the previous commit.

Refinement is now its own `Kind` instead of a `Custom` with a display label,
because the page needs the scope and the edit list.

The sidebar is 240px and each row is two lines: name, short id, a copy button
(which copies the full id and does not open the session), then turns and file
size. Peak and compaction counts moved to the detail page. A "≥ 轮" filter at
the top of the sidebar hides sessions below a turn threshold; it defaults to 1
and persists in localStorage. 77 of 119 session files hold only a few
metadata rows, and they buried the ones worth reading.

Three counts were wrong, and one was lying about its unit:

1. The overview said "平均 243 轮/次" next to the compaction count. 243 is
   entries per compaction (56k entries / 232 compactions), not turns; in turns
   it is 2.7. Relabelled to 条目/次.
2. The timeline column "间隔轮数" counts assistant calls (median 94), not
   turns. Renamed to 间隔调用, and the help text now says why the two differ by
   an order of magnitude.
3. The new turn count is user messages (628), so the overview now says 对话轮数
   and reports the *median* calls per turn rather than the mean: 444 of 627
   turns are under 25 calls and one is 1,419, so "35 calls per turn" describes
   almost no turn at all.

`callsPerTurn` also reports `silent`: 44 of the 628 turns were user messages
that another user message immediately followed, so the model never answered
them. 628 = 584 answered + 44 queued, and the payload asserts that sum.